! Entrance block ~ the record

The law reads at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/entrance-block`>>. This record keeps how it arrived and what it still owes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/grounds`>>

!! The grounds ~ two scouts, 2026-07-11

Two tasked spirits read two domains on 2026-07-11 and reached the coupling law independently, sharing no vocabulary: cardiology (the Arnol'd tongues hold nonzero measure for arbitrarily small coupling, so no safe epsilon stands) and physarum (the tube contractions organize into a network-wide peristaltic wave, and the shared cytoplasm couples the oscillators whether or not anyone wills it). The same day the operator ruled one sovereign body per stream.

The first framing read //"the rhythms MUST NOT entrain"//. The gankogui reading sharpened it to the law the api meme states: forbid the phase, never the period.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed ~ what the canon has not yet paid for

''`embed_io` stands untested against the WAIT.'' The warm embedder rides as a shared holder — //"the model is the resource"// — and every stream reaches it. A stream that POINTS at the holder clears the shore; a stream that BLOCKS on it couples through the queue. ''Test it, or give each body its own embedder and pay the memory.''

Every shared resource in the py fleet owes the same test: `content_io` · `structurepalace_io` · `form_store` · the WAL · the drain ledger. ''The question never reads "does it carry payload." It reads "does a stream WAIT on it."''

<<~/ahu>>

